1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,128
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:06,589
[COUNTDOWN TICKING]

3
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:10,135
<i>- Surprise!</i>
<i>- Surprise!</i>

4
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:11,052
[CHUCKLING]

5
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:13,138
[PRECIOUS]<i> Billy, you are</i>
<i>behind all this, aren't you?</i>

6
00:00:13,221 --> 00:00:15,140
[GUESTS SINGING]
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>

7
00:00:15,223 --> 00:00:18,393
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

8
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,647
[DRAMATIC BEAT]

9
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:25,525
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

10
00:00:27,902 --> 00:00:29,320
[PHONE BEEPS]

11
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:33,908
[PHONE BEEPS]

12
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:37,662
[PHONE BEEPS]

13
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:42,500
<i>Billy! Oh my God!</i>

14
00:00:44,502 --> 00:00:45,545
<i>Are you okay?</i>

15
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:48,298
<i>You know him, Auntie?</i>

16
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:49,632
<i>Uh…</i>

17
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,468
<i>Yes. That's Sir Eric.</i>

18
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:54,179
<i>I was planning</i>
<i>to tell you about him, Billy.</i>

19
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:57,307
<i>Billy, I can explain.</i>

20
00:00:58,516 --> 00:01:01,853
<i>You even made a fool of the person</i>
<i>who raised us and cared for us</i>

21
00:01:01,936 --> 00:01:03,938
<i>when that should have been you?!</i>

22
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:05,690
[PRECIOUS]
<i>He's your father, Billy?</i>

23
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:07,484
<i>Leave.</i>

24
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:09,319
<i>You're a liar!</i>

25
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,155
<i>- Precious--</i>
<i>- I said leave!</i>

26
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:14,616
<i>Never show your face here again! Leave!</i>

27
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:15,700
<i>Get out!</i>

28
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:16,910
<i>Are you okay?</i>

29
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:24,501
<i>We're tired of waiting on you, Enrico.</i>

30
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,753
<i>I don't care anymore.</i>

31
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:28,421
<i>You want to beat me up?</i>

32
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,590
<i>Just kill me!</i>

33
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:33,843
<i>If you really can't pay</i>
<i>the money back, fine.</i>

34
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:35,804
<i>I'll get it from your daughter.</i>

35
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:38,139
- [ENRICO GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

36
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:40,767
- [KICKS LAND]
- [PAINED GROANS]

37
00:01:42,393 --> 00:01:44,687
<i>If you dare go anywhere near my children,</i>

38
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:47,565
<i>- I'll kill you!</i>
- [GROANS]

39
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:49,692
<i>Do you understand?!</i>

40
00:01:50,652 --> 00:01:52,070
[WHIMPERS, GROANS IN PAIN]

41
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:54,531
[OLIVER SINGING ON VIDEO CALL]
<i>♪ Happy birthday ♪</i>

42
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:56,491
<i>♪ To you ♪</i>

43
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:57,575
<i>Love you.</i>

44
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:01,579
[PRECIOUS]
<i>What if he keeps bothering you?</i>

45
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:04,958
<i>What if he tells Oliver the truth?</i>

46
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:06,876
[BILLY] <i>Oliver, let's talk.</i>

47
00:02:07,877 --> 00:02:12,173
<i>You want to study at Kingsley</i>
<i>because of our father, right?</i>

48
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:14,467
<i>It's not true that he's dead.</i>

49
00:02:16,177 --> 00:02:18,179
<i>I didn't tell you because</i>

50
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:19,347
<i>he abandoned us,</i>

51
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:21,307
<i>and I didn't want you to get hurt.</i>

52
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:23,893
<i>Where is he?</i>

53
00:02:24,602 --> 00:02:29,482
<i>You know Sir Eric,</i>
<i>the guy you met at school?</i>

54
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,734
<i>He is our father.</i>

55
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:35,655
<i>And just because you're mad at him,</i>

56
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:38,074
<i>you want me to lose a father?!</i>

57
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:40,827
<i>I don't get it, Billy!</i>

58
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:47,584
[CRYING, MUMBLING INDISTINCTLY]

59
00:02:55,091 --> 00:02:57,218
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

60
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:12,775
Oliver?

61
00:03:22,493 --> 00:03:24,203
Open the door, please.

62
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,788
Let's talk.

63
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:30,043
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:30,126 --> 00:03:31,920
Oliver, baby boy.

65
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:34,047
Can we please talk?

66
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,469
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

67
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:42,013
Oliver.

68
00:03:53,816 --> 00:03:55,401
Billy.

69
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:57,528
Let me handle this, okay?

70
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:01,241
Maybe he's still mad.

71
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,492
I got this, okay?

72
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:05,703
Oliver?

73
00:04:08,122 --> 00:04:10,458
Oliver, baby boy, come on.

74
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:12,210
Please open the door.

75
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:19,342
He still won't talk to you?

76
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:26,266
Oliver?

77
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,268
It's Bro Dude.

78
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:30,270
Talk to me.

79
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:31,771
Come on.

80
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:35,400
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

81
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:46,244
[MOUTHS SILENTLY]

82
00:05:01,301 --> 00:05:02,343
Buddy,

83
00:05:03,928 --> 00:05:05,513
your sister loves you so much.

84
00:05:06,097 --> 00:05:07,473
That's why she did that.

85
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:13,730
Really?

86
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:22,655
Do you think it's okay to keep secrets
from someone you love?

87
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:27,160
She lied to me.

88
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:41,799
Your dad also lied to you.

89
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:43,968
[OLIVER SIGHS]

90
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:47,013
Of course you would side with Billy.

91
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:48,473
No, Oliver.

92
00:05:49,348 --> 00:05:50,892
I'm not siding with anyone.

93
00:05:50,975 --> 00:05:51,809
Come here.

94
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,106
Look,

95
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:01,069
I'm not saying
what your sister did was right.

96
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:03,446
But I understand her.

97
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:05,740
She's just trying to protect you.

98
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:07,533
Okay?

99
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:09,994
She knows what your father is like.

100
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:13,039
Well, good for her.

101
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:15,166
Because I don't.

102
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,752
Bro Dude,

103
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:21,547
didn't you say your father left you too?

104
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:24,717
If he came back

105
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,260
and reached out to you,

106
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:28,971
wouldn't you want to talk to him?

107
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:35,812
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

108
00:06:36,979 --> 00:06:38,106
I don't know.

109
00:06:39,565 --> 00:06:46,280
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

110
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:26,904
[DINO] Family is the Lord's
most important gift.

111
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:30,992
- [MAN] Amen.
- [DINO] So remember to take care of them.

112
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:32,869
To value them.

113
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,455
And to love them.

114
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:36,789
Never hurt your family.

115
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:37,957
[MAN] Amen.

116
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:39,917
[DINO] I…

117
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:42,170
I deeply regret

118
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,672
what I did to my children

119
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:46,674
and to my wife.

120
00:07:47,383 --> 00:07:49,427
But I believe

121
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:50,761
that it is not too late.

122
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:51,846
Amen.

123
00:07:54,599 --> 00:07:55,558
There is still hope.

124
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:58,811
Change and forgiveness are possible.

125
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:01,105
Have faith, my brothers.

126
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:05,943
Let us pray that we are given the chance

127
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:08,196
to make it up to the people we love.

128
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:09,280
- Amen.
- Amen.

129
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:14,785
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:08:14,869 --> 00:08:16,871
That's all I want.

131
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:19,290
To talk to Papa.

132
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:21,459
You know,

133
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:24,921
I have a lot of questions for him.

134
00:08:26,964 --> 00:08:30,134
Can't Billy answer them for you?

135
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:32,887
No.

136
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:37,808
Because I want to ask him.

137
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:40,019
I want him to answer my questions.

138
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:47,652
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:09,382
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

140
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:12,969
Auntie and I are here if you want to talk.

141
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:17,390
I'm not leaving you for Papa.

142
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:20,059
I just want to talk to him.

143
00:09:20,142 --> 00:09:26,023
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

144
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:29,527
He would only tell you lies, Oliver.

145
00:09:31,862 --> 00:09:33,781
He left us, didn't he?

146
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,744
What's left to talk about?

147
00:09:40,204 --> 00:09:41,914
Please, Billy. No.

148
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:45,376
Let me speak to Papa.

149
00:09:45,459 --> 00:09:48,170
Let me decide if

150
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:50,339
he is a good person

151
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:51,507
or a bad one.

152
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:53,342
Please, Billy. Please.

153
00:09:54,802 --> 00:10:01,559
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

154
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:10,985
He just needs time.

155
00:10:14,071 --> 00:10:15,281
Thank you.

156
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:19,744
I'll help you with Oliver.

157
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:21,912
I'll keep trying.

158
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:23,748
He'll understand.

159
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:28,753
Am I wrong?

160
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:34,800
I mean, we're the same.

161
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:37,428
I still can't forgive my dad either.

162
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:41,474
But you love Oliver.

163
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:42,892
That's all that matters.

164
00:10:47,396 --> 00:10:50,566
[DOORBELL RINGING]

165
00:10:55,946 --> 00:10:57,406
Let's talk, Precious.

166
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:58,699
Please.

167
00:10:59,992 --> 00:11:01,827
We have nothing else to talk about.

168
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:04,121
I know everything now. You can go.

169
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:05,790
Aren't you ashamed?

170
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:07,541
You didn't just use me.

171
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:09,460
You even lied to Oliver!

172
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:15,216
You've got some nerve, coming here!

173
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:16,384
Billy.

174
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:18,052
Oliver knows the truth.

175
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:20,221
I also told the school
about your real identity,

176
00:11:20,304 --> 00:11:22,431
so you can no longer work there.

177
00:11:22,515 --> 00:11:25,935
And you don't have a family
anymore either.

178
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:29,188
Dear, just hear me out.

179
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:31,982
Please, just go.

180
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:36,070
Billy.

181
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:40,574
[FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

182
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:50,084
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:03,389
<i>Pa?</i>

184
00:12:05,307 --> 00:12:07,351
<i>- Pa! Pa.</i>
<i>- Hey…</i>

185
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:10,312
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:11,897
<i>A brand-new car?</i>

187
00:12:11,981 --> 00:12:13,774
<i>Is that ours?</i>

188
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:14,733
<i>Yes.</i>

189
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:16,652
<i>Now we can go on as many trips as we want.</i>

190
00:12:16,735 --> 00:12:18,696
<i>You miss your sister, don't you?</i>

191
00:12:18,779 --> 00:12:22,199
<i>Well, now we have a car</i>
<i>to visit her in Manila.</i>

192
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:24,243
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

193
00:12:24,326 --> 00:12:25,327
<i>Manila?</i>

194
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:26,454
<i>So when are we leaving?</i>

195
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:27,997
<i>- Today!</i>
- [GIGGLES]

196
00:12:29,248 --> 00:12:30,583
<i>We're going right now?</i>

197
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:32,710
<i>- Yes, so let's go!</i>
- [STAMMERS]

198
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:34,378
<i>- Your mother's all dressed up.</i>
<i>- Yeah, she is!</i>

199
00:12:34,462 --> 00:12:36,964
<i>Okay, I won't bother changing then!</i>
[GIGGLES]

200
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:39,300
<i>- Here, I brought some clothes.</i>
<i>- Let me help you.</i>

201
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:40,968
[YOUNG BEA] <i>Oh, really? Thanks, Ma!</i>

202
00:12:41,051 --> 00:12:42,428
<i>Oh…</i>

203
00:12:42,511 --> 00:12:43,471
<i>- Ma?</i>
<i>- Hmm?</i>

204
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:45,139
<i>- Can I take the front seat?</i>
<i>- Nuh-uh.</i>

205
00:12:45,222 --> 00:12:46,432
<i>- You can't.</i>
<i>- Okay then.</i>

206
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:47,808
<i>You can sit there.</i>

207
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:52,521
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

208
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:53,647
[MARIELA GRUNTS]

209
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:55,858
[YOUNG BEA GIGGLES]

210
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:57,067
<i>Okay?</i>

211
00:12:57,151 --> 00:12:58,360
[ENGINE STARTS]

212
00:12:58,444 --> 00:12:59,320
<i>- Let's go!</i>
<i>- Ready?</i>

213
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:01,238
<i>- We're ready!</i>
<i>- Where do you want to go?</i>

214
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:02,364
<i>First stop.</i>

215
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:03,365
<i>A convenience store.</i>

216
00:13:03,449 --> 00:13:05,242
<i>- Convenience store! Let's go!</i>
<i>- My goodness…</i>

217
00:13:05,326 --> 00:13:07,703
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

218
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:11,123
<i>How are we feeling? Are we happy or what?</i>

219
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:12,625
<i>Yes, Pa!</i>

220
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:14,919
<i>- That's good, then.</i>
<i>- Does Abi know?</i>

221
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:16,045
<i>- Nope.</i>
<i>- </i>[GASPS] <i>What?</i>

222
00:13:16,128 --> 00:13:17,922
<i>- She won't expect it.</i>
<i>- We're going to surprise her?</i>

223
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:19,173
<i>- That's right!</i>
- [GIGGLES]

224
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:20,382
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

225
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:22,009
<i>By the way, where is her office again?</i>

226
00:13:22,092 --> 00:13:23,344
[LAUGHTER]

227
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:24,970
<i>All I know is that</i>
<i>it's somewhere in Manila.</i>

228
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:26,680
<i>We haven't gotten her a present yet.</i>

229
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:29,308
[YOUNG BEA]<i> Let's go</i>
<i>to a convenience store first.</i>

230
00:13:29,391 --> 00:13:31,769
<i>Pa, we've been driving for ages.</i>

231
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:33,812
<i>- Maybe we can stop for now.</i>
<i>- The food's better in Manila.</i>

232
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:36,148
<i>- Let's just buy food there.</i>
<i>- She's hungry already.</i>

233
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:38,067
<i>- Hungry already?</i>
<i>- Of course!</i>

234
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:40,986
<i>But we haven't gotten very far at all!</i>

235
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:43,572
<i>Well, that's just how it is.</i>
<i>We should've brought some food.</i>

236
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:45,783
<i>Then we'd have been able</i>
<i>to have something to eat</i>

237
00:13:45,866 --> 00:13:49,245
<i>while listening to our favorite song</i>
<i>during the trip.</i>

238
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:50,704
<i>What was it again?</i>

239
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:51,956
<i>I don't know. You tell me.</i>

240
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:53,457
[LAUGHTER]

241
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:55,084
<i>Who's going to sing it?</i>

242
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,878
<i>- I will! I'm the singer!</i>
<i>- Okay, okay, okay.</i>

243
00:13:57,962 --> 00:13:59,380
<i>- </i>[MARIELA]<i> All right.</i>
<i>- Take the lead. Go!</i>

244
00:13:59,463 --> 00:14:05,844
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

245
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:12,893
[MUSIC FADING]

246
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:18,274
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:20,401
I hesitated at first, Abi.

248
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:29,410
I wasn't sure if…

249
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:34,248
it was really Papa I saw in the video.

250
00:14:34,331 --> 00:14:38,419
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,546
I wanted to be sure, so…

252
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:44,300
I went to Billy's house.

253
00:14:50,514 --> 00:14:51,432
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

254
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:53,559
Just taking a chance.

255
00:14:53,642 --> 00:14:58,898
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,024
And sure enough…

257
00:15:04,361 --> 00:15:05,487
I saw him.

258
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:10,868
[SNIFFLES]

259
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:14,204
It was Papa.
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

260
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:17,875
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

261
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:19,251
I saw him.

262
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:28,177
[SNIFFLING, CRYING]

263
00:15:29,511 --> 00:15:31,096
You know what, Abi?

264
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:36,602
He went to see Billy first,

265
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:40,147
before even coming to his own family.

266
00:15:41,815 --> 00:15:42,858
[SNIFFLES]

267
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:45,611
[INHALES, EXHALES SHARPLY]

268
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:48,238
[SNIFFLING]

269
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:50,699
[SIGHS]

270
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:54,954
What does Papa think of us, Abi?

271
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:58,874
[SNIFFLES]

272
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,543
Why does he treat us this way?

273
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:02,753
[BREATH QUIVERING]

274
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:06,006
[SNIFFLES]

275
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:08,133
What are we to him?

276
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:12,554
Trash?

277
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,182
[SNIFFLES]

278
00:16:15,265 --> 00:16:16,517
Just trash.

279
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,645
That's all we are to him.

280
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:22,481
[SNIFFLES]

281
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:23,816
Trash.

282
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:28,404
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

283
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:29,863
[SNIFFLES LIGHTLY]

284
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:36,704
[CRYING QUIETLY]

285
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:41,000
[SNIFFLES, WHIMPERS]

286
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:50,300
[CRYING, SNIFFLING]

287
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:57,391
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

288
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:10,612
[EXHALES SHAKILY]

289
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:15,034
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

290
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:24,960
[SNIFFLES]

291
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:29,798
[SNIFFLING]

292
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:43,395
[MUSIC TURNS EMOTIONAL]

293
00:17:53,572 --> 00:18:00,412
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

294
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:09,880
[MARIELA]
<i>Call your sister. Let's eat.</i>

295
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:14,468
[PLATES CLATTERING]

296
00:18:14,551 --> 00:18:17,930
<i>Ma, why are there only three plates?</i>

297
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:22,101
<i>I told you to call your sister.</i>

298
00:18:23,143 --> 00:18:25,521
<i>Did you know she got promoted?</i>

299
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:29,691
<i>- Hmm?</i>
<i>- Your sister is really amazing.</i>

300
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:32,820
<i>She's so smart.</i>

301
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:35,531
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

302
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:36,657
<i>Come on, Ma.</i>

303
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:39,076
<i>I was just asking why</i>
<i>there were only three plates,</i>

304
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:41,578
<i>and you keep blabbing about Abi.</i>

305
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:43,539
<i>So why are there only three plates?</i>

306
00:18:43,622 --> 00:18:46,625
<i>Is Papa not coming home?</i>
<i>Isn't he joining us?</i>

307
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:51,880
<i>You are so dumb, aren't you?</i>

308
00:18:51,964 --> 00:18:53,549
<i>You're stupid!</i>

309
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:56,135
<i>You really take after your father.</i>

310
00:18:56,218 --> 00:18:57,928
<i>You're both useless!</i>

311
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:00,347
<i>So, what?</i>

312
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:04,059
<i>Are you going to take his side? Huh?</i>

313
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:07,771
<i>Then get out of here and go with him!</i>

314
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:11,608
<i>You deserve each other anyway!</i>

315
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:14,486
[MARIELA SCREAMING]

316
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:15,529
[PLATE SHATTERS]

317
00:19:15,612 --> 00:19:19,241
- [MARIELA SCREAMING]
- [PLATES SHATTERING]

318
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:24,705
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

319
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:27,708
<i>What happened?</i>

320
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:35,465
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

321
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:47,853
[FIRE CRACKLING]

322
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:51,398
[ABIGAIL] <i>Ma! Ma!</i>

323
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:54,276
[SCREAMING]

324
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:56,528
[FIRE CRACKLING]

325
00:19:56,612 --> 00:19:58,197
[GASPS, COUGHS]

326
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,328
- [THUD]
- [ABIGAIL WHIMPERS]

327
00:20:04,411 --> 00:20:05,245
<i>Ma!</i>

328
00:20:06,788 --> 00:20:07,915
<i>Ma!</i>

329
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:09,875
[DOOR THUDS]

330
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:16,840
[FIRE CRACKLING]

331
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:19,927
[WOOD THUDS]

332
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:24,932
[FLAMES HISSING]

333
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:26,099
Ma! Ma!

334
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:28,268
[MARIELA COUGHS]

335
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:29,811
[HUSHED] <i>Ma.</i>

336
00:20:29,895 --> 00:20:31,939
- [MARIELA GROANS]
- [ABIGAIL GRUNTS]

337
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:32,981
<i>- Oh my God!</i>
<i>- Help!</i>

338
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:35,192
<i>Ma! Ma!</i>

339
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:36,568
<i>- Take her.</i>
<i>- Ma.</i>

340
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,528
<i>- Help her.</i>
<i>- Help! Ma.</i>

341
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:42,616
<i>Ma, wake up! Ma!</i>

342
00:20:42,699 --> 00:20:43,951
[BEA CRYING]

343
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:44,993
<i>Ma.</i>

344
00:20:45,535 --> 00:20:46,995
[LABORED BREATHING]

345
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:49,456
<i>- Abigail! Abigail!</i>
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

346
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:52,000
<i>Abigail! Abigail!</i>

347
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:54,336
- [ABIGAIL BREATHING HEAVILY]
<i>- Abigail.</i>

348
00:20:54,419 --> 00:20:55,629
<i>Abigail.</i>

349
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:57,714
<i>Abigail.</i>

350
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:00,050
<i>Abigail!</i>

351
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:06,098
[NURSE] <i>It's done.</i>

352
00:21:08,976 --> 00:21:10,852
<i>Your father has abandoned us.</i>

353
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:13,063
<i>He has a new family in Manila.</i>

354
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:17,359
<i>He cheated on me. He cheated on us!</i>

355
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:20,279
<i>He chose his mistress</i>

356
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:23,365
<i>and their illegitimate child!</i>

357
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:26,618
<i>They are to blame for your sister's death!</i>

358
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:30,664
<i>Damn them. Damn all of them.</i>

359
00:21:30,747 --> 00:21:33,667
<i>Damn them!</i>

360
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:40,048
[MARIELA CRYING]

361
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:42,342
[MARIELA WHIMPERS]

362
00:21:43,218 --> 00:21:46,221
- [MARIELA SNIFFLING]
- [BEA WHIMPERING]

363
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,931
[MARIELA BREATHES SHAKILY]

364
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:51,393
[MARIELA CRYING]

365
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:01,028
- [ENRICO]<i> You bought a lot, huh?</i>
<i>- Daddy! </i>[GIGGLES]

366
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:02,321
<i>Pa?</i>

367
00:22:02,404 --> 00:22:03,739
[GIRL AND ENRICO GIGGLING]

368
00:22:03,822 --> 00:22:05,324
- [WOMAN] <i>We're so happy.</i>
- [BEA] <i>Pa.</i>

369
00:22:05,407 --> 00:22:06,908
<i>Pa. Pa!</i>

370
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:08,577
<i>Pa.</i>

371
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:10,245
<i>Pa!</i>

372
00:22:14,499 --> 00:22:16,918
<i>Let me speak to Papa first.</i>

373
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:19,046
<i>That man you think is kind to you</i>

374
00:22:19,129 --> 00:22:21,715
<i>is the reason our mother died.</i>

375
00:22:21,798 --> 00:22:24,676
<i>Auntie, I understand why</i>
<i>he would feel this way.</i>

376
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:26,803
<i>But I can't give him what he wants.</i>

377
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:29,431
<i>Dude?</i>

378
00:22:29,514 --> 00:22:31,141
<i>Oliver's still mad.</i>

379
00:22:31,224 --> 00:22:33,477
<i>- Sir Jordan, your grandpa…</i>
<i>- What's wrong?</i>

380
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:35,145
<i>- He escaped.</i>
<i>- What?!</i>

381
00:22:35,937 --> 00:22:38,023
<i>- Jordan?</i>
<i>- Grandpa Jude is missing.</i>

382
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:39,608
<i>All right, I'm on my way.</i>

383
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:41,151
<i>You still haven't found my grandpa?!</i>

384
00:22:41,234 --> 00:22:42,903
<i>Sir, we're very, very sorry.</i>

385
00:22:42,986 --> 00:22:44,279
<i>Jordan!</i>

386
00:22:44,362 --> 00:22:46,573
<i>Dude, I can't find him.</i>

387
00:22:47,532 --> 00:22:49,576
<i>Please, I can't lose him too.</i>
